{
  "file": "crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs",
  "item": "impl[CachedProvider/SourceProvider]/fn[read]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "The provider overrides parse with a cached snapshot. Selected-source\n reads must deliver and fingerprint that snapshot without fetching again;\n this trait-required callback rejects a refetch. Primitive provider reads\n are covered separately, and executing this guard would fail this test."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation is on an explicit function with a body, `impl[CachedProvider/SourceProvider]/fn[read]` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs`. That is a permitted target. The justification is fenced citation commentary, so it is a tracked explanation rather than an ordinary comment.\n\nThe explanation is substantive and agrees with the source:\n- `CachedProvider` overrides `parse` in `impl[CachedProvider/SourceProvider]/fn[parse]` to return a cached snapshot through `parse_snapshot`. It does not call `read`.\n- The default `parse` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources.rs#mod[defaults]/fn[parse]` calls `provider.read`. `read` is therefore a required trait method that this fixture deliberately turns into a guard, and it returns `SourceError::Invalid(\"must not refetch\")`.\n- The test `cached_selected_source_reads_record_exact_delivered_contents_and_errors_add_no_input` runs `search_structure`, `outline_source` and `read_source` through `SourceTools` with `CachedProvider`. It asserts that the recorded dependency fingerprint is the cached `fn observed() { call(); }` content. If the guard ran, the test would fail. Zero execution of `read` is therefore the intended outcome, not a coverage hole.\n- The claim that primitive provider reads are covered elsewhere is plausible. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs` has providers whose `read` returns real data, such as `impl[Primitives/SourceProvider]/fn[read]`. The same file also uses an equivalent justified guard on `CachedParse`.\n\nThe item has no {impl} or {test} reference to the same declaration, so the citation is not redundant. The citation's stated criteria are met.",
